WEBVTT

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
♪

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.020
♪

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:30.020
♪

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:36.020
Oh, this is the best torpedo I have tasted,

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.020
I don't know, since the last time we were here together.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.020
This whole day has been a pleasant surprise for me, Carolyn.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.020
You held up even better than a torpedo.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.020
Oh, bless you, Robert,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.020
you're still the backhanded compliment champion of San Francisco.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.020
Uncontested.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.020
Only, now that I'm in a wheelchair,

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.020
people feel guilty when they get an overwhelming desire to knock me on my backside.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.020
But you never fooled me.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.020
Under that grouchy hide beats the heart of a beautiful tyrant.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.020
That's why I proposed to you several light years ago.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.020
It's a pity you turned me down.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:24.020
A tyrant can never accept someone else's suggestion,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.020
no matter how good it is.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:46.020
♪

00:02:46.020 --> 00:03:09.020
♪

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:15.020
When you called this morning,

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:21.020
you said you wanted to wallow in a little nostalgia.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.020
But there's something else on your mind, what is it?

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:29.020
♪

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:34.020
Jason left me Friday night.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.020
We're getting a divorce.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.020
Why?

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:43.020
Marriage was a mistake.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.020
Two people don't stay together this long unless they've got something going for them,

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:55.020
even if it's a mutual desire to be miserable.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:00.020
Ma'am, I'd like to talk to you for a minute, chief, alone.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.020
Excuse me.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.020
Yes, certainly, Robert.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:14.020
♪

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.020
Well, I wanted to...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.020
Jason White's office called headquarters this morning.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.020
White didn't show up for work today.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:27.020
There's some evidence that he's been murdered by Mrs. White.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:34.020
♪

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:07.020
♪

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:17.020
♪

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:27.020
♪

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:32.020
Yes, I've been seeing another woman for almost a year now.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.020
I love her, Carolyn.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.020
Oh, don't make me laugh, Jason.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.020
You're incapable of loving anybody but yourself.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.020
You're the most egotistical man I ever met.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.020
As long as you feel that way, there should be no problem.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:52.020
You can file the action, on the grounds of mental cruelty, if you like.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.020
Never.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.020
I'll file it myself.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.020
You can't hold me.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:00.020
You know that better than I do.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.020
You're kidding.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.020
What are you doing with that gun?

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:10.020
Put it away, Carolyn, before somebody gets hurt.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.020
Carolyn!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.020
I don't understand.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:25.020
There was no gun, there were no shots fired.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.020
Did you argue with him?

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.020
Oh, yes, yes, Friday night, just the way you heard it.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:33.020
Up to the part about the gun, that never happened.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.020
And we argued at home, not here.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.020
How do you explain the bloodstains on the carpet?

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:41.020
I don't know how they got there, or even what they mean.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.020
What's your theory?

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.020
I have none.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:57.020
I think they mean Jason White was shot to death in this office.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.020
I'd say that's the sound of Jason White's corpse being dragged out of the office.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:06.020
The stain over here would indicate the murder of Pauls, while holding the body to open the door.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:11.020
There's a groove in the carpet, as if a man's heel had been dragged through it.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:16.020
If you think I killed my husband, Sergeant, it's your duty to tell me and advise me of my rights.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.020
When was the last time you saw Jason?

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.020
Friday night.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:25.020
After the argument, he packed a few things and left.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.020
Do you own a gun?

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.020
Yes.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.020
Where's the gun now?

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.020
On the night table by my bed.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:39.020
I'd like you to go home and get it.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:51.020
Carolyn, if Jason is alive, we'll find him, I promise you.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:56.020
I lose more blood than that when I get a quick shave at the office.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.020
Sure.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.020
Excuse me.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:07.020
Thank you.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.020
I thought I turned that thing off.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.020
You did, just before you got turned off.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:13.020
We just made another recording of her voice.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:17.020
I want the sound lab to make a comparative analysis of the two.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:20.020
All things being equal, her voice quality should be the same on both.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.020
Unless Carolyn White is telling the truth.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:27.020
How do we determine that?

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.020
We deduce, determine, and decide.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:37.020
It's called detective work.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.020
He used another machine and then transferred the teeth.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:42.020
Or he could have returned for the machine after everyone had gone,

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:46.020
reported the argument at home, and then brought it back Saturday.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.020
If Mrs. White argued with her husband at home Friday night,

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:52.020
and that was the last time she saw him, what was she doing here Saturday morning?

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.020
How do you know she was here?

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:57.020
I took her up in the elevator around a quarter to twelve.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.020
I remember because it was just before lunchtime.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:02.020
I was clock-watching.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.020
Did you take her down again?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.020
No. She must have come down herself while I was out.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.020
Did you see Mr. White?

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:13.020
No, but he usually comes in before I do on Saturdays.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:17.020
And his car was in the basement garage when I punched in that morning.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:20.020
His car is not there now.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:25.020
But there is a large blood stain in his parking space.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:32.020
If he drives a two-door sedan parking head-in, the trunk door would open just about here.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:37.020
While the lab is analyzing these stains, contact White's personal physician.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:42.020
He probably has a blood test we can compare them with.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:49.020
You know, sir, for a man who simply cut himself shaving, White lost a lot of blood.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.020
You're absolutely certain he's dead?

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.020
Well, everything points in that direction.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:56.020
She confronted her husband. He admitted he was seeing another woman.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:59.020
Why was the argument so conveniently recorded?

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:03.020
Well, Jason must have figured she was going to say something he could use against her in divorce court.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.020
So he turned on the recorder without her knowing about it.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:09.020
That part you've got to buy, Chief. You just had me pull the same stunt.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.020
Very logical.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:19.020
But none of you has proved that Jason White is dead.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.020
We received a report, Chief.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:25.020
One of our units found this abandoned vehicle here.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:29.020
It's registered to Jason White.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:35.020
None of these keys work.

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:39.020
Chief, that's not my bag anymore. Remember?

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:42.020
Open the trunk.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:11:04.020
Would you mind?

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.020
Another blood stain.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:08.020
I don't know where the body is buried, but it was taken there in this trunk.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.020
And by a woman.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:13.020
Eve, you better see how Carolyn is doing with the gun.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.020
It's a dress button.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.020
The material looks expensive, and it's covered with blood.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:23.020
The same type blood they found on the carpet and in Jason White's parking space.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:25.020
Did the lab check with his doctor?

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:29.020
Yes. White's blood characteristics are identical to those found in the stains.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:34.020
Hello, Carolyn.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:39.020
Bob.

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.020
Bob, my gun's missing.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.020
We looked everywhere. No sign of it.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.020
Did you go to Jason's office, Sandra D?

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.020
Yes.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.020
Why?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.020
Well, he called me and wanted me to meet him there.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.020
But I never saw him.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.020
When I got there, the office was empty.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:03.020
So I waited about, oh, half an hour, and then I left.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:06.020
Were there any signs in the house that Mr. White had left?

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:09.020
If he went anywhere, he was planning to come back soon.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:13.020
All his shaving gear is intact, and there are two wardrobe closets full of his clothing.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:18.020
I did find something interesting, though, in Mrs. White's closet.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.020
There's a fresh stain on this dress.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:24.020
It looks like dried blood that's been partially washed off with cold water.

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:47.020
The button is missing.

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:50.020
I don't understand it, Bob, and neither does the D.A.'s office.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.020
Why haven't you booked Carolyn White for murder?

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.020
I want more time.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:57.020
There are too many shadows in this case, not enough substance.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:02.020
I'd like to remind the chief that corpus delicti can be established without the murder weapon.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:04.020
Or the victim's body.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.020
I can get a conviction tomorrow on just what you've got.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:11.020
It's the day after tomorrow I'm worried about, Clayton. What's going to turn up then?

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:12.020
Probably more of the same.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:15.020
Every piece of evidence we have so far points at Carolyn.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:19.020
The record of her argument with Jason, her missing gun,

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.020
the blood-stained button in the trunk of her car.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.020
All of it circumstantial.

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:26.020
Okay, this type of case is not easy to prosecute,

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:30.020
but it has been done in this state and successfully.

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:35.020
If you rush Carolyn White to court, I have a feeling we're all going to wind up with egg in our faces.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.020
Your conduct during this investigation isn't helping matters.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.020
What do you mean by that?

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.020
You've been biased in her behalf from the very beginning.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.020
Clayton, that's a lie.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.020
Oh, come off it, Ironside.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:48.020
Everybody knows she's an old friend of yours.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:51.020
It wouldn't matter if she was a complete stranger or my little old grandmother.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.020
She'd still get the same shake.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.020
Commissioner, you have the reports on the chief's preliminary interrogations,

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:01.020
but you can see for yourself they may have put me at a serious disadvantage.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.020
Why didn't you notify her immediately that she was a suspect in form of her rights?

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:08.020
Because I chose not to.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:13.020
Well, your touching faith in Mrs. White may just get half our brief thrown right out of court.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:15.020
She told you she had a gun.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.020
She told you she went to Jason's office.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:20.020
Now, both of those statements were self-incriminating.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:23.020
I'd say her rights were never violated.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:26.020
Bob, you're close to her. Very close.

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:33.020
Maybe it would be better if you laid off the case.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:37.020
Commissioner, I've been bending rules and busting criminals for 20 years on this force.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:15:06.020
If my honesty and my methods can't be trusted anymore, maybe it's time to quit.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.020
Molly, good.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:10.020
Now, I want you in it to check Jason White's ledgers.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.020
If you want my personal opinion, I think that Mrs. White is just playing guilty

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.020
and that you're too emotionally involved to see it.

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:19.020
Your opinion is shared by everybody, but there's nothing wrong with my objectivity.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.020
On the contrary, I'm trying to go beyond the obvious, and that's why I'm in the minority.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.020
Okay, let's talk about attitudes.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:28.020
I think that she's acting like a wife who knows that her husband is dead,

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:31.020
and she could only know that if she killed him.

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:33.020
What makes you think she knows he's dead?

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.020
She's too cool, too composed.

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:39.020
If she was sure he was dead, then she would be in a state of great anxiety.

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:42.020
How many psychology courses did you take in college?

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.020
One, basic psychology.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:48.020
All right, if Carolyn is such a cool, calculating woman,

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:51.020
why did she kill Jason minutes after she was seen by the elevator operator?

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:53.020
Murder was committed in the heat of an argument.

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:55.020
The recording indicates that.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:58.020
And if she shot Jason in his office, she must have brought the gun from home where she always kept it.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.020
And she killed him in cold blood.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.020
Planned the whole thing.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.020
Now you're contradicting yourself.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:07.020
What was it, passion or premeditated murder?

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.020
Well, make up your mind.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:15.020
I don't know. I'm not sure.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.020
You've got to be sure.

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:19.020
Now, you said Carolyn was just plain guilty.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.020
I'm still a woman, and my instincts tell me that there is something wrong

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.020
with the way she's taking this whole thing.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:29.020
Women's instincts are what make them the world's lousiest detectives.

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:32.020
I got the report from the sound lab.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:35.020
The recording of the argument, the recording you made,

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.020
were both made on the office dictating machine.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.020
That doesn't guarantee they were both made in the office.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.020
Chief, you sure die hard.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.020
Look, Ed, I played the recordings again.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.020
There's less traffic noise in the background of the argument.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.020
That could mean it took place in Jason's home.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.020
In a quiet residential area.

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:53.020
It could also mean it did take place in the office.

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:55.020
I checked the traffic in the legal district.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:57.020
It's very quiet on Saturdays.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:17:00.020
A lot lighter than it was on Monday when you made the second recording.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:03.020
So it's a standoff. We can both be right.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.020
Well, yes, sir. No, no, sir.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.020
Not when you add up all the other elements.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:11.020
Easy think. Simple conclusions based on obvious facts.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.020
What is it you want us to think?

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.020
Everything. Keep all the possibilities alive,

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:19.020
but don't jump to any conclusions till you have all the facts.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:22.020
Are you still playing with the idea Jason White's alive?

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.020
I'm playing with the idea that this is all too easy.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.020
And Carolyn White is not a stupid woman.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:31.020
And it's your educated opinion that she's innocent.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:34.020
I'm not interested in educated opinions, yours or mine.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:38.020
I want the truth. The pure, hard-to-find truth.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.020
And I suppose it's up to us to find it for you.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:45.020
Now, that is an intelligent piece of deductive reasoning.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:47.020
I never heard them argue.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.020
Oh, come on, Miss Danny. Tell us the truth.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:54.020
Mrs. White is a very easy person to get along with.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:56.020
She's a wonderful woman.

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:58.020
How often did she come in?

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.020
Almost every day.

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:02.020
She did Mr. White's briefs for him.

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:06.020
She also did his research and investigation work.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:09.020
And they never had a fight in all these years.

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:13.020
You'd better tell us what you know.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:17.020
I heard them shout at each other in his office,

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.020
but only once in a while. It wasn't important.

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:23.020
Married people do fight, you know.

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.020
What about?

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:28.020
They don't like to see their names on other people's arguments.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.020
Then how do you know they weren't important?

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.020
Did Mr. White have many women clients?

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.020
Yes, most of them.

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:38.020
They all thought he was very charming.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:42.020
Do you remember anyone in particular who used to call him a lot?

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.020
No. There were too many.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.020
I'd like the log of all the incoming and outgoing calls,

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.020
also the appointment calendar.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:52.020
And a complete list of all his clients, please.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.020
How did you discover the recording?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.020
I use a dictating machine every Monday.

00:18:56.020 --> 00:19:00.020
He usually comes in alone on Saturdays and leaves dictation for me.

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:03.020
Did Mr. White take the machine with him when he went home Friday night?

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.020
No, I was using it when he left.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:08.020
That'll be all. Thank you.

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:10.020
Not at all.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.020
Hello, Robert.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.020
Carolyn, you've met your future colleague, Mr. Sam.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:19.020
Yes, hello, Mark. How's the law been treating you?

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:23.020
I get a little time off for good behavior.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.020
My father used to say,

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:28.020
the law is the sternest of taskmasters.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.020
Well, he was almost right.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.020
Talking about the bar makes me thirsty.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:35.020
Boris, a drink, will you, Mark?

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:37.020
Make something mild for Mrs. White.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.020
Sit down, Carolyn.

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.020
I hope you'll indulge me.

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:44.020
Of course.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:46.020
What is it?

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:48.020
I haven't asked this before.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.020
Did you kill Jason?

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:57.020
I thought you believed in my innocence.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:20:02.020
After 20 years in the force, I've got an occupational disorder.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:05.020
I'm never absolutely certain about anything.

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:08.020
Even when I'm dead sure.

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.020
I didn't.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:16.020
I didn't. We argued.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.020
But I didn't kill him.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.020
When he left the house that night, he was alive.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:22.020
And he wasn't in his office on Saturday.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:24.020
I'll swear to that, Hunter-Oath.

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:26.020
That won't be necessary.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:28.020
Thank you.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:36.020
I prayed you'd say that.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:48.020
I think I'll see how those drinks are coming.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:53.020
I'll be back.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.020
Something wrong?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:02.020
I'd rather have you spit it out than choke on it.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:09.020
You may know a lot of things, boss, but I knew a con job when I saw one.

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:12.020
You know what you have to see, Mark.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:18.020
It makes a con job work.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:33.020
How could such a tough, uncompromising pro be so sweet?

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:37.020
Rarely a day passes I don't ask myself the same question.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.020
Me too.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.020
Shall we get to work?

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.020
Right now.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:48.020
Before Randall changes his mind and deactivates my pension.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:50.020
Thank you.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:57.020
Where did you find out Jason was seeing another woman?

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:59.020
You know women, Robert.

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:04.020
I guess I suspected sometime last year.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:08.020
But I wasn't sure until a few months ago.

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:12.020
You waited a long time before you confronted him with it.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:15.020
Ego.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:19.020
I hoped he'd have his little mid-40 fling and then return to his senses.

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:22.020
Did you ever get the urge to check up on him?

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:25.020
No.

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:28.020
What good would it have done?

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:31.020
I didn't want to torture myself.

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:37.020
Knowing a woman's name, seeing her face, knowing where they met.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:40.020
Carolyn.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:47.020
What kind of woman does he find attractive?

00:22:47.020 --> 00:22:50.020
He prefers the tall ones.

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:52.020
Shapely.

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:54.020
Athletic.

00:22:54.020 --> 00:22:56.020
And he likes them young.

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:01.020
Yes, I would say definitely she was a young woman.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:04.020
Gee, I think I've got something.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:08.020
I missed Erickson just before each one of Mr. White's business trips.

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:10.020
Erickson, do you know her?

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:13.020
No, I don't think she's a client of Jason's.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:17.020
No, she's not. I found a number listed in his telephone book alongside one of her calls.

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:19.020
She probably left a return number.

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:21.020
It's a photographer's studio.

00:23:21.020 --> 00:23:23.020
She's a model.

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:25.020
Her professional name is...

00:23:25.020 --> 00:23:29.020
Candy Erickson. Real smorgasbord.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:32.020
Tasty dish. All mixed up.

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:36.020
Beautiful, elegant, nutty. You know what I mean.

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.020
You name it, she's got it.

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:41.020
Did Miss Erickson ever discuss any of her boyfriends with you?

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:46.020
Talking to Candy about her social life is like discussing troop movements with the Army Chief of Staff.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:48.020
But lately she's been playing house with only one guy.

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:50.020
Do you know his name?

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:53.020
No, she never mentions it. But if I know Candy, he's a player with lots of money.

00:23:53.020 --> 00:23:55.020
When was the last time you saw her?

00:23:55.020 --> 00:23:58.020
Last Thursday. I sent her out on a job.

00:23:58.020 --> 00:24:02.020
I've been calling her all this week, but there's no answer.

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:03.020
Is she in trouble?

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:05.020
We don't know yet.

00:24:05.020 --> 00:24:08.020
Well, the chick's unreliable. She still owes me money.

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:12.020
She bought some fancy sailing outfits that she was modeling and charged them to the agency.

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:16.020
Could you give us her address and all the photographs you can spare?

00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:20.020
Oh, well, she got that stuff at cost.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:22.020
She skipped town. At least I'm not out the retail price.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:25.020
You know what a markup there is on those rags?

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:28.020
Sailing outfits are not here.

00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:30.020
Did Miss Erickson leave word that she was going out of town?

00:24:30.020 --> 00:24:33.020
No, but she's always off someplace.

00:24:33.020 --> 00:24:35.020
Just hops in that little car of hers and away she goes.

00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:37.020
Sometimes I don't see her for days.

00:24:37.020 --> 00:24:42.020
Did you ever see her in the company of an older man, distinguished-looking, gray hair, around 40?

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:46.020
You're asking me to remember one pine tree in a forest.

00:24:46.020 --> 00:24:48.020
Jason's been very discreet.

00:24:48.020 --> 00:24:53.020
Apparently he and Candy always arranged to meet secretly at some permanent rendezvous somewhere close,

00:24:53.020 --> 00:24:55.020
yet where they wouldn't be recognized.

00:24:55.020 --> 00:24:59.020
That would eliminate most places in the Bay Area, including the marinas,

00:24:59.020 --> 00:25:02.020
if they went sailing together.

00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:09.020
When a girl has a wardrobe like Candy's, she doesn't use a sailing outfit unless she goes sailing.

00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:12.020
I agree with you. The question is, where did they go?

00:25:12.020 --> 00:25:15.020
Now, the chief would pick up a book like this and say,

00:25:15.020 --> 00:25:23.020
I wrote Tamar and other poems with love from J.

00:25:25.020 --> 00:25:28.020
Rhone Stallion, also by Jeffers.

00:25:30.020 --> 00:25:33.020
And then he'd say, that's it!

00:25:33.020 --> 00:25:36.020
Robinson Jeffers lived in the Big Sur and he wrote about it.

00:25:36.020 --> 00:25:39.020
There's a hundred miles of mountain wilderness along that coastline,

00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:42.020
and it's less than two hours from here by car.

00:25:42.020 --> 00:25:45.020
Then he'd be right.

00:25:47.020 --> 00:25:52.020
The label in this dress. Mickey's, Big Sur, California.

00:25:52.020 --> 00:26:12.020
So that's how he does it.

00:26:53.020 --> 00:26:57.020
The Big Sur

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:09.020
Try the public officials in the merchants.

00:27:09.020 --> 00:27:11.020
Someone in these parts is bound to recognize them.

00:27:11.020 --> 00:27:14.020
Right, Chief. Ed's already started on it.

00:27:14.020 --> 00:27:17.020
No, I can't say I've seen either of them.

00:27:17.020 --> 00:27:20.020
Thanks. We've got a lot of territory to cover.

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:23.020
Can you borrow a car? You bet.

00:27:25.020 --> 00:27:28.020
If I knew a man like that, I'd grab him for myself.

00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:31.020
I'm tired of slinging hamburgers for a living.

00:27:32.020 --> 00:27:35.020
I don't get to see many people in this job.

00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:38.020
I spend most of my time looking for the smoke.

00:27:38.020 --> 00:27:40.020
Thanks.

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:43.020
Yeah, I know that couple. The Jays.

00:27:43.020 --> 00:27:45.020
They buy the goods here every once in a while.

00:27:45.020 --> 00:27:47.020
When was the last time you saw them?

00:27:47.020 --> 00:27:50.020
Oh, about a month ago, I guess. Do you know where they live?

00:27:50.020 --> 00:27:52.020
Yeah, they bought the old McIntyre place.

00:27:52.020 --> 00:27:55.020
It's in a little cove down by the ocean, Chief.

00:27:55.020 --> 00:27:58.020
Continue south on the Coast Highway for about 12 miles.

00:27:58.020 --> 00:28:00.020
I'll be waiting there for you. Good work, Eve.

00:28:00.020 --> 00:28:02.020
I'll round up the others.

00:28:02.020 --> 00:28:04.020
Notify Ed to meet us there.

00:28:04.020 --> 00:28:07.020
But first I want him to dig up whatever he can on the Jays.

00:28:07.020 --> 00:28:17.020
Right, Chief. Over and out.

00:28:38.020 --> 00:28:40.020
It doesn't look as if anybody's here.

00:28:40.020 --> 00:28:42.020
Those tire tracks are fairly new.

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:45.020
Narrow, probably made by a sports car.

00:28:45.020 --> 00:28:49.020
Eve, check out the boat while we have a look around the house.

00:28:49.020 --> 00:29:09.020
Right. I found the door open.

00:29:09.020 --> 00:29:34.020
All right, Mark, see what's in the bedroom.

00:29:34.020 --> 00:29:35.020
Lipstick.

00:29:35.020 --> 00:29:54.020
Yes. Could be Candy Erickson's. It's a good shade for a blonde.

00:29:54.020 --> 00:30:05.020
See if that's still fresh.

00:30:05.020 --> 00:30:08.020
Yes.

00:30:08.020 --> 00:30:11.020
It is Mark's Saturday.

00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:17.020
Somebody was definitely here over the weekend.

00:30:17.020 --> 00:30:20.020
No freezer compartment.

00:30:20.020 --> 00:30:22.020
So?

00:30:22.020 --> 00:30:24.020
Those waffles are the frozen kind.

00:30:24.020 --> 00:30:44.020
There must be a freezer around here someplace.

00:30:44.020 --> 00:30:48.020
Meat, vegetables, TV dinners.

00:30:48.020 --> 00:30:51.020
Frozen food to last two people for a year.

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:55.020
Most of it has been put here the last few days.

00:30:55.020 --> 00:30:57.020
Are you sure?

00:30:57.020 --> 00:31:01.020
Yeah, there's very little frost on it.

00:31:01.020 --> 00:31:24.020
Packs on the bottom are covered with the stuff.

00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:31.020
I found these hanging in the closet. Two women sailing outfits and some men's clothing.

00:31:31.020 --> 00:31:34.020
Those are Jason's. They were here together.

00:31:34.020 --> 00:31:39.020
Probably Saturday, the day you supposedly shot Jason at the office.

00:31:39.020 --> 00:31:47.020
It would take more than a milk carton to prove it.

00:31:47.020 --> 00:31:48.020
What did you find?

00:31:48.020 --> 00:31:57.020
Candy Erickson. Her body was floating under the dock.

00:32:19.020 --> 00:32:33.020
Are you going to arrest Mrs. White?

00:32:33.020 --> 00:32:34.020
No.

00:32:34.020 --> 00:32:36.020
It's an obvious case of double murder.

00:32:36.020 --> 00:32:38.020
We've got one of the bodies now to prove it.

00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:40.020
There's still a body missing.

00:32:40.020 --> 00:32:46.020
Until we find Jason or some other answers, he remains a prime suspect and the case remains open.

00:32:46.020 --> 00:32:51.020
Shame. Pretty old gal like that.

00:32:51.020 --> 00:32:53.020
You can help, Sheriff.

00:32:53.020 --> 00:32:56.020
I want you to put out an all-points apprehend order for Jason White.

00:32:56.020 --> 00:32:59.020
All right. I'll get after it right away.

00:32:59.020 --> 00:33:04.020
And, Sheriff, lean on your coroner.

00:33:04.020 --> 00:33:07.020
I want an A to Z autopsy and I need the results ten minutes ago.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:13.020
I'll do what I can.

00:33:13.020 --> 00:33:16.020
Take the car and question every grocer in the area.

00:33:16.020 --> 00:33:22.020
I have a hunch Jason bought milk, eggs and a large supply of frozen food sometime Saturday morning.

00:33:22.020 --> 00:33:25.020
The elevator operator said that Jason was in his office Saturday morning.

00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:28.020
She saw his car, but she never saw Jason.

00:33:28.020 --> 00:33:31.020
I'll start with the locals first.

00:33:31.020 --> 00:33:34.020
No, ma'am. I couldn't have sold any of those things to anybody.

00:33:34.020 --> 00:33:37.020
I'm not even open on Saturday.

00:33:37.020 --> 00:33:40.020
Have you been over to old John Bella's place?

00:33:40.020 --> 00:33:43.020
He don't care what day it is as long as he's making money.

00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:47.020
He's got a dinky little general store. It sits way back in the woods over there.

00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:51.020
I don't stock frozen goods. You couldn't get me to eat that stuff and I'm not about to sell it.

00:33:51.020 --> 00:33:56.020
It's a hopeless rocket. You and I both know that.

00:33:56.020 --> 00:33:59.020
Why don't we let the district attorney do his job?

00:33:59.020 --> 00:34:05.020
Not yet. I have a feeling something will turn up.

00:34:05.020 --> 00:34:10.020
You really think so? Yes, I think so.

00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:15.020
I hope you're right.

00:34:15.020 --> 00:34:21.020
Meanwhile, I want to go over it again. I want it straight. All of it.

00:34:21.020 --> 00:34:23.020
All right, Robert.

00:34:23.020 --> 00:34:27.020
Jason could have sued for divorce if he merely wanted to be rid of you.

00:34:27.020 --> 00:34:33.020
But a man has to have a stronger reason than that to play dead for the rest of his life.

00:34:33.020 --> 00:34:38.020
What do you have on him?

00:34:38.020 --> 00:34:41.020
He bribed a juror on his last case. And?

00:34:41.020 --> 00:34:45.020
And I, uh... All of it?

00:34:45.020 --> 00:35:14.020
I threatened to expose him.

00:35:14.020 --> 00:35:16.020
I've checked every possible angle.

00:35:16.020 --> 00:35:20.020
If Jason was stashing money away, he sure didn't leave any tell-tale signs.

00:35:20.020 --> 00:35:22.020
A big spender like him would need plenty of ready cash, chief.

00:35:22.020 --> 00:35:25.020
Especially if he was planning on getting lost the rest of his life.

00:35:25.020 --> 00:35:29.020
What about the local bank? Nothing. Under White, Jay, or any other name.

00:35:29.020 --> 00:35:35.020
How'd he pay for the boat? Cash. The house, too. Bought them outright under the name Jay.

00:35:35.020 --> 00:35:40.020
That proves he had money that was unaccounted for. The puzzle is, where did he hide it?

00:35:40.020 --> 00:35:45.020
Carolyn, did Jason ever keep money in the office safe?

00:35:45.020 --> 00:35:47.020
No. Just some petty cash and strongbox.

00:35:47.020 --> 00:35:51.020
There was no strongbox in it when I checked it Monday. You think he brought it here with him?

00:35:51.020 --> 00:35:55.020
You and Mark look around. If he's traveling light, he might have dumped it somewhere before he took off.

00:35:55.020 --> 00:35:57.020
Right. Finders keepers.

00:35:57.020 --> 00:36:01.020
Don't get excited. You'll be lucky enough to find it. And if you do, there won't be any money in it.

00:36:01.020 --> 00:36:06.020
Then I'll go digging around the beach. At least I can add to my shell collection.

00:36:06.020 --> 00:36:10.020
If Jason planned all this, his scheme looks flawless.

00:36:10.020 --> 00:36:14.020
But when you get up close, you discover nothing's that perfect.

00:36:29.020 --> 00:36:33.020
Did you find the money box? No, but I got a lot of sand in my shoes.

00:36:33.020 --> 00:36:37.020
What's new that's good? Nothing. The highway patrol found Candy's car this morning.

00:36:37.020 --> 00:36:41.020
Carolyn's.22 pistol was in the glove compartment, and her fingerprints are on it.

00:36:41.020 --> 00:36:44.020
Well, that should just about have wrapped things up for Clayton.

00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:46.020
Shall we give up the ghost?

00:36:46.020 --> 00:36:50.020
When I'm ready to quit, I'll throw in the towel.

00:36:50.020 --> 00:37:10.020
In the meantime, keep looking.

00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:13.020
There's no longer any doubt about it, Ironside.

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:15.020
The bullets were removed from Candy's brain.

00:37:15.020 --> 00:37:18.020
Ballistics tests prove they were fired from her gun.

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:21.020
If that's all you've got to tell me, you can skip along back to court.

00:37:21.020 --> 00:37:24.020
Not quite. You're off the case.

00:37:24.020 --> 00:37:26.020
With the commissioner's blessing.

00:37:26.020 --> 00:37:29.020
A warrant for Mrs. White's arrest.

00:37:29.020 --> 00:37:33.020
She's charged with the murder of Candy Erickson, and this one I can make stick.

00:37:33.020 --> 00:37:35.020
With hard, physical evidence.

00:37:35.020 --> 00:37:40.020
I'm sorry, Carolyn. I think this is a bad mistake.

00:37:40.020 --> 00:37:43.020
Don't blame yourself. You've done all you can.

00:37:43.020 --> 00:37:45.020
Not by a long shot.

00:37:45.020 --> 00:37:50.020
You're beaten, Robert. I'm tired, and I'm beaten.

00:37:50.020 --> 00:38:10.020
Take me back to San Francisco. I'm ready to face the charges.

00:38:10.020 --> 00:38:17.020
I found fresh dirt covering a sump hole, so I dug it up. It's empty.

00:38:17.020 --> 00:38:22.020
Jason's empty money box is hardly proof that he's alive, or that he framed his wife.

00:38:22.020 --> 00:38:26.020
It's a start.

00:38:26.020 --> 00:38:28.020
Hey, word on Jason?

00:38:28.020 --> 00:38:31.020
Trace. The bulletin's out, and all my deputies on it.

00:38:31.020 --> 00:38:32.020
Keep them on it.

00:38:32.020 --> 00:38:39.020
Here's your autopsy report. Knock that out in a big hurry, just like you asked.

00:38:39.020 --> 00:38:44.020
Two lungs killed instantly by the first of two bullet wounds in the brain, and dumped in the ocean.

00:38:44.020 --> 00:38:48.020
You won't find any evidence in there that'll clear Mrs. White.

00:38:48.020 --> 00:38:53.020
Don't bank your case on it.

00:38:53.020 --> 00:38:57.020
This report says Candy's been dead for approximately 48 hours.

00:38:57.020 --> 00:38:59.020
Today's Wednesday.

00:38:59.020 --> 00:39:05.020
It means Candy was murdered sometime Monday afternoon, while Mrs. White was in San Francisco.

00:39:05.020 --> 00:39:12.020
That's more than an alibi, Chief.

00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:15.020
I can't believe it.

00:39:15.020 --> 00:39:27.020
I just talked to Eve on the radio. She's with someone she thinks we'd all like to meet personally.

00:39:27.020 --> 00:39:31.020
You were right, Chief. Jason White was buying groceries Saturday morning.

00:39:31.020 --> 00:39:35.020
He was in about noontime, or a little before. Bought a few things. Milk, eggs...

00:39:35.020 --> 00:39:36.020
And frozen vegetables.

00:39:36.020 --> 00:39:42.020
Not that time, no, sir. Milk, eggs, coffee, and some bread. That's all.

00:39:42.020 --> 00:39:50.020
He couldn't possibly have been in his office when Mrs. White was supposed to have killed him.

00:39:50.020 --> 00:39:53.020
Are you absolutely sure it was the same man?

00:39:53.020 --> 00:40:02.020
Oh, yes, sir. I know Mr. J pretty good. Most times he comes in, he buys a whole mess of frozen food.

00:40:02.020 --> 00:40:04.020
Well, I don't know what to think now.

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:07.020
An empty money box? A dead girlfriend Mrs. White couldn't have killed?

00:40:07.020 --> 00:40:10.020
And now an eyewitness who saw him when he was supposed to be dead.

00:40:10.020 --> 00:40:20.020
Jason must be in hiding somewhere. Guilty of conspiracy to frame his wife and murder.

00:40:20.020 --> 00:40:28.020
I'm going back to San Francisco. My office will request the court to dismiss charges against Mrs. White.

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:32.020
Congratulations, Mrs. White.

00:40:32.020 --> 00:40:40.020
I... I don't know how to thank all of you.

00:40:40.020 --> 00:40:50.020
Congratulations, Mrs. White. Congratulations.

00:41:11.020 --> 00:41:14.020
Hello, Robert.

00:41:14.020 --> 00:41:17.020
Sit down, Carla.

00:41:23.020 --> 00:41:25.020
What is it?

00:41:25.020 --> 00:41:28.020
I'm sorry, it's not going to work.

00:41:28.020 --> 00:41:30.020
What?

00:41:30.020 --> 00:41:37.020
You planted two sets of evidence. The first to prove your guilt, the second, the alibis to prove your innocence.

00:41:37.020 --> 00:41:40.020
Robert, now how can you make such a horrible joke?

00:41:40.020 --> 00:41:45.020
By carefully incriminating yourself, you made it look like Jason had framed you.

00:41:45.020 --> 00:41:48.020
Certainly no one would suspect you of framing yourself.

00:41:48.020 --> 00:41:50.020
Robert, what are you saying?

00:41:50.020 --> 00:41:57.020
The dictating machine from Jason's office Friday night baited him into an argument at home and secretly recorded it.

00:41:57.020 --> 00:42:04.020
He asked you for a divorce. You pulled a gun. He told you to put it away and you did.

00:42:04.020 --> 00:42:13.020
After he left to meet Candy at the office, left his car in the garage and drove with her to the cabin, you edited the recording.

00:42:13.020 --> 00:42:21.020
The part where you put the gun away was erased. Gunshots and the sound of a body being dragged across the floor, you added.

00:42:21.020 --> 00:42:25.020
You returned the machine that night, knowing it would be played first thing Monday.

00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:27.020
The frame.

00:42:27.020 --> 00:42:33.020
Saturday morning you went back to the office again and made sure the elevator operator saw you.

00:42:33.020 --> 00:42:35.020
The alibi.

00:42:37.020 --> 00:42:42.020
When you got to the cabin, Jason was out shopping.

00:42:44.020 --> 00:42:46.020
The girl was alone.

00:42:48.020 --> 00:42:50.020
You killed her.

00:42:50.020 --> 00:42:52.020
Well, that's impossible.

00:42:52.020 --> 00:42:54.020
And when Jason returned, you killed him too.

00:42:54.020 --> 00:42:56.020
Oh, Robert, stop this.

00:42:56.020 --> 00:43:01.020
Sunday morning you planted the blood, the ditched car and the missing button.

00:43:01.020 --> 00:43:06.020
Look, it's not true, any of it. I didn't kill Jason and I couldn't have killed Candy.

00:43:06.020 --> 00:43:10.020
You saw the autopsy report. I was in San Francisco when she was shot.

00:43:11.020 --> 00:43:18.020
The autopsy determines the time of death by the amount of decomposition present when the body is examined.

00:43:18.020 --> 00:43:22.020
You suspended the process by placing Candy's body in the freezer.

00:43:22.020 --> 00:43:26.020
You took it out Sunday night and dumped it in the ocean.

00:43:26.020 --> 00:43:30.020
Making it appear Candy Erickson was killed around noon on Monday.

00:43:30.020 --> 00:43:33.020
It's pure supposition.

00:43:33.020 --> 00:43:40.020
Look, Robert, what are you expecting from me? A confession?

00:43:40.020 --> 00:43:43.020
Frankly, Carolyn, I am.

00:43:43.020 --> 00:43:46.020
Well, even if it were true, you couldn't prove it.

00:43:46.020 --> 00:43:48.020
Why?

00:43:48.020 --> 00:43:50.020
Why?

00:43:54.020 --> 00:43:56.020
Why would you do it?

00:44:06.020 --> 00:44:09.020
Suppose, just suppose, mind you.

00:44:09.020 --> 00:44:13.020
Suppose there were other beach houses and other girls.

00:44:13.020 --> 00:44:15.020
Would it make more sense then?

00:44:15.020 --> 00:44:18.020
A divorce would have made more sense.

00:44:18.020 --> 00:44:24.020
And suppose, suppose I really loved him, in spite of the beach houses.

00:44:24.020 --> 00:44:28.020
You know, when you love a man that much, you hang on, even if there's nothing left but pain.

00:44:28.020 --> 00:44:31.020
I don't consider murder hanging on.

00:44:31.020 --> 00:44:35.020
Oh, you forget? No murder. Only supposition.

00:44:36.020 --> 00:44:38.020
Facts.

00:44:38.020 --> 00:44:43.020
A laboratory analysis will prove some of the food in that freezer had been defrosted and refrozen

00:44:43.020 --> 00:44:45.020
before you dumped Candy's body in the ocean.

00:44:45.020 --> 00:44:47.020
Jason did that.

00:44:47.020 --> 00:44:49.020
Jason's dead.

00:44:49.020 --> 00:44:50.020
Then find his body.

00:44:50.020 --> 00:44:53.020
We found it. Under the money box.

00:44:53.020 --> 00:44:55.020
About three feet further down.

00:44:55.020 --> 00:45:02.020
When a man is looking for something buried, he usually stops at the first thing he finds.

00:45:02.020 --> 00:45:07.020
It never occurs to him that something else might be buried deeper.

00:45:10.020 --> 00:45:14.020
Candy's body is a very important piece of evidence.

00:45:14.020 --> 00:45:17.020
It's a very important piece of evidence.

00:45:17.020 --> 00:45:20.020
It's a very important piece of evidence.

00:45:20.020 --> 00:45:25.020
It's a very important piece of evidence.

00:45:25.020 --> 00:45:27.020
Carolyn?

00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:36.020
First, you give up your life's work.

00:45:36.020 --> 00:45:39.020
And then your life.

00:45:39.020 --> 00:45:42.020
And in return, you wait at home.

00:45:42.020 --> 00:45:47.020
And you pretend not to notice the smudge of lipstick on his shirt.

00:45:47.020 --> 00:45:52.020
Or the strange cigarette butts in the ashtray of his car.

00:45:52.020 --> 00:45:59.020
You look a thousand different directions, avoiding seeing what a fool you are.

00:46:01.020 --> 00:46:07.020
And then one day, he tells you he's had it.

00:46:07.020 --> 00:46:10.020
He's had it.

00:46:10.020 --> 00:46:12.020
Him.

00:46:12.020 --> 00:46:15.020
Tell me, Robert.

00:46:15.020 --> 00:46:17.020
What was he?

00:46:17.020 --> 00:46:20.020
What is a Jason White?

00:46:20.020 --> 00:46:23.020
Without me, nothing.

00:46:23.020 --> 00:46:28.020
I shaped him. I molded him. I created him.

00:46:28.020 --> 00:46:32.020
And for thanks, he used me.

00:46:36.020 --> 00:46:40.020
Human beings do that sometimes.

00:46:40.020 --> 00:46:43.020
Use the people that love them.

00:46:43.020 --> 00:46:45.020
Granted.

00:46:45.020 --> 00:46:50.020
But they don't have to be proud of themselves for doing it.

00:46:50.020 --> 00:46:56.020
Oh, Jason was more than proud. Yes, he thought he was a genius.

00:46:56.020 --> 00:46:59.020
Well, he learned differently.

00:46:59.020 --> 00:47:05.020
Yes, he learned we're not all such fools as he thought.

00:47:05.020 --> 00:47:10.020
He understood it all very clearly at the end.

00:47:10.020 --> 00:47:15.020
Carol, you understand your rights?

00:47:15.020 --> 00:47:41.020
Only too well.

